    "Adjust forecasts downward when sentiment history shows negative sentiment (e.g., -0.25 or 0.00) and true prices show strong downward momentum.",
    "Reduce forecast overshoot after sharp price spikes by applying a 1-2 day lag correction to prevent overreaction.",
    "Apply mean reversion bias correction: if forecast is > 10% above recent 5-day average, reduce by 5-10% unless sentiment is bullish.",
    "Increase forecast sensitivity to recent low prices when sentiment is neutral or negative — especially if true price has recently fallen below 65.",
    "When true price drops below 60, reduce forecast by 5-10% to avoid overestimating rebound potential.",
    "If sentiment history includes 0.33 or higher, increase forecast volatility by 5% to reflect bullish momentum, but cap at 10% above recent peak."
